# Local stale snapshots of this repo, untracked on purpose: they are a pre-0.4.8 copy whose
# commit is already in main's history, and 125k files here must never reach `git add -A`.
raven_old*/

# `raven/core/memory/long_term.py` writes an agent's notes (`general.md`, `lessons.md`, `project.md`,
# `user.md`) under the process's working directory, so a gateway started from a checkout puts what one
# person wrote about their own work where `git add -A` reaches it. Anchored to the root: an unanchored
# `memory/` would also hide `raven/core/memory/` and `raven/plugins/memory/`, where real modules live.
/memory/

# Session exports the chat UI writes into the working tree are conversation transcripts, not
# documentation. One weighed 46,412,860 bytes; a later one named `raven!!!.md` (1,665,107 bytes)
# reached a public commit anyway, because the rule here remembered the exporter's naming convention
# (`<topic>_<date>_<hh-mm>.md`) and that file had been renamed by hand. A name cannot be predicted, so
# root Markdown is opt-in instead: publishing a new root doc takes its own `!` line, a deliberate act,
# while a transcript under any name stays out. `docs/` is untouched and keeps its own dated files.
/*.md
!AGENTS.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
!CONTRIBUTING.md
!README.md
!README.ru.md
!SECURITY.md
